+# Supplier Invoice Details presentation — FRO-348
+
+Controlled, unconnected React presentation for the approved comfortable Details design. This is partial preparation: no invoice route, service, wire model, authority, persistence, source picker, form controller or live operation is delivered. Existing Order invoice rows are unrelated.
+
+## Composition and data ownership
+
+- `SupplierInvoiceDetailLayout` uses existing Card, TopBar, Badge and Tabs with a local keyboard wrapper, saved-value grids and one controlled editor surface. `fields.saved` contains authorized, already formatted values. `fields.editor` contains the actual labelled controls supplied by the eventual TanStack Form controller; the layout does not coerce or format them. The parent owns the active card, all draft values and saved snapshots outside conditionally mounted panels. Refs restore focus to Edit when the parent resolves the active editor. Null document count means unknown, not zero.
+- `SupplierInvoiceVatSummary` displays supplied saved status and dates. Its stage is a presentation discriminant, not an API enum or a calculation from type/VAT/events. Historical saved wording remains unchanged. Only the three qualifying stages show the noninteractive progression and dates. No fourth progress step is introduced. Action slots must already be authorized and disabled/omitted by the caller when prerequisites or other work block them.
+- `SupplierInvoiceConfirmation` uses the real Modal/Button/Alert primitives. It adds an accessible modal name locally, preserves focus trap/restoration, and forwards Confirm only for supplied idle/eligible state. Pending blocks dismissal and submission; rejected, stale and unknown do not imply success. Unknown optionally exposes a supplied original-attempt check. The parent retains dates/action/payload/precondition/attempt context even after dismissal and resets rejection to idle only after required review/correction. Nested calendars/dropdowns must consume their Escape before the outer modal. Callbacks do not implement server idempotency.
+- `SupplierInvoiceRelationship` renders supplied Entry Note/Export states separately: unavailable, loading, error, denied, conflict, confirmed absence and ready content. Only ready receives authorized links and metadata. Caller owns cancellation/invalidation and ignores stale results for previous Orders; this component never fetches or infers relationships.
+- `SupplierInvoiceSavedDocuments` mirrors shared saved-attachment presentation with Card/Button/feedback. It consumes invoice-owned metadata and supplied row-specific download callbacks; it does not use the existing PO/Shipment AttachmentPanel ownership, services, permissions, upload or removal actions. Only a ready empty collection means no saved documents. Download absence does not imply absence of the saved file.
+
+All imports use the actual `#/` alias and current `src/components/ui/` files. New compositions are saved-value cards, VAT progression, confirmations/outcomes and relationship/file state presentation. Existing AppShell is unchanged. Component-local EN/EL copy uses the current labels provider. Caller-supplied content, saved status, dates, errors and metadata must also be localized and accessible. Controls must use real FormField/Input/DatePicker/Combobox/Select or the existing TanStack Form field components; no native fixture control substitutes for production behavior.
+
+## Required controller and contract work
+
+FRO-321 must deliver invoice identity, staff/record/action access, reads, exact-decimal/date/duplicate validation, atomic Order/dependent correction, cancellation/events, concurrency/read preconditions, audit, original-attempt reconciliation and invoice-owned list/download contracts. No authority name or endpoint is assumed here. Current GraphQL Float amounts cannot establish lossless invoice money transport.
+
+FRO-356 supplies explicit Order regime; do not infer it from warehouse, VAT or Entry Note. The complete form/controller must supply authorized searchable Order/currency/vessel options, protected type corrections and the focusable unavailable storage-option reason extension. The extension and source picker are not implemented by this presentation.
+
+FRO-317/FRO-321 supply explicit Export membership, positive IE599 and shared invoice events; FRO-319 supplies admission-aware direct/inherited Entry Note lookup. Their later integrations remain explicitly unavailable until delivered and do not become confirmed absence. FRO-347 terminology is shared, but its unmerged presentation branch is not a dependency of this change.
+
+Full invoice retrieval, route access/cache clearing, guarded in-app navigation, reload/unload warning, retained invoice controller, server validation, successful-operation invalidation (including old/new Order presence), original-attempt recovery and source/permission guarantees remain unimplemented. No data is stored durably by these components. Hidden UI is not authorization. Supply capabilities from the future authoritative controller; never expose a production route with fixtures or default-allowed actions.
+
+## Verification scope
+
+Retained tests cover exact caller-owned text across tabs/locale, keyboard tabs, editor/control gating, supplied saved VAT stages, confirmation cancellation/uncertainty and callbacks, relationship distinctions and saved-file download rows. Browser fixtures render these actual components and mapped primitives at desktop and narrow widths. They prove controlled presentation only, not backend persistence, fiscal eligibility, staff scope or successful business operations.
+
+Run existing client test/build/format/type checks; see the planning handoff for exact results, inherited failures, browser evidence and complete patch. No GraphQL source changes or generated-reference work are introduced. No migration, backend, dependency, shared primitive, route/navigation, infrastructure or deployment change belongs to this preparation.
